# No browser work without explicit consent

Do not perform browser-related work unless the user has explicitly agreed in the current conversation.

This includes:

- Opening, navigating, or controlling a browser (MCP browser tools, Playwright, Puppeteer, Selenium, etc.)
- Taking screenshots or snapshots of pages for debugging
- Clicking, typing, or interacting with live UI
- Installing browser automation tooling to investigate UI issues

When browser inspection would help, ask first. Describe what you would check and wait for approval.

Without consent, use non-browser approaches instead: read code, run API/CLI tests, check server logs, ask the user to share console errors or screenshots.
